{
  "baseVariant": "first compact-table batch, before compact builder",
  "builderVariant": "compact style-ID run builder",
  "platform": "macOS 15.7.9 arm64",
  "method": "One fresh process per case, classic Nim c -d:release --mm:arc, identical dependencies and checkpoint harness; MallocStackLogging=1, paused after storage or first render; leaks --fullStackHistory --outputGraph=<file> <pid>, malloc_history <file> -highWaterMark -callTree -invert -ignoreThreads -consolidateAllBySymbol and without -highWaterMark. Units reported by Apple malloc_history as MB/M/GB are preserved verbatim; its no-stack blocks and VM regions are separate.",
  "limitations": [
    "One traced run per case; logging overhead and allocation scheduling perturb memory and timings.",
    "malloc_history reports a dynamically-enabled logging warning with 816 pre-existing unstacked blocks for storage and 805 blocks plus 9 VM regions for view; totals exclude unstacked allocations.",
    "Process heap/RSS/high-water are separate from logged live allocation heap and VM, and do not identify retained objects.",
    "Graphs and full call trees are local artifacts in /tmp/merenda-utf8-profile; graph files include full stack history and are not checked into the repository.",
    "Per-sample targetStages includes measurements after the graph checkpoint (such as resized); these later stages are not represented in the captured graph."
  ],
